<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Explicit Jailbreak Distribution</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now give the explicit construction of the jailbreak distribution
<math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{{jb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{{jb}}</annotation></semantics></math> and its probability mass.
Let <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">main_jb</span> be a base jailbreak instruction, and let
<math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{s_{1},\dots,s_{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{s_{1},\dots,s_{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of side jailbreak instructions.
We split <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">main_jb</span> into consecutive sentences
<math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},\dots,m_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},\dots,m_{K})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The jailbreak <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is then formed as an alternating sequence of
main and side instructions:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=(m_{1},k_{1},m_{2},k_{2},\dots,m_{K})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=(m_{1},k_{1},m_{2},k_{2},\dots,m_{K}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of side instructions
inserted between <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, for each gap <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,K-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,K-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each side instruction <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is included in
<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> independently with probability <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}(\eta)\subseteq\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}(\eta)\subseteq\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the chosen subset,
its elements are permuted uniformly at random, i.e., each ordering
has probability <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/|T_{j}(\eta)|!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/|T_{j}(\eta)|!</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the probability of generating a jailbreak <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\eta)\;=\;\prod_{j=1}^{K-1}\Bigg[\Bigg(\prod_{s\in T_{j}(\eta)}\rho\Bigg)\Bigg(\prod_{s\in\mathcal{S}\setminus T_{j}(\eta)}(1-\rho)\Bigg)\frac{1}{|T_{j}(\eta)|!}\Bigg]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\eta)\;=\;\prod_{j=1}^{K-1}\Bigg[\Bigg(\prod_{s\in T_{j}(\eta)}\rho\Bigg)\Bigg(\prod_{s\in\mathcal{S}\setminus T_{j}(\eta)}(1-\rho)\Bigg)\frac{1}{|T_{j}(\eta)|!}\Bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This defines <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{{jb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{{jb}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is used in the
main analysis as a black-box sampling distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
